<protocol name="compliance_research" type="decision" domain="product">

## PURPOSE

Guide regulatory research for HSN classification, compliance requirements, and certification needs. Ensure products are catalog-ready with correct classifications and compliance awareness.

---

## CORE PRINCIPLE: COMPLIANCE IS CATEGORY-DEPENDENT

> **Not all products need compliance research. The PRODUCT TYPE determines requirements.**

| Category | Compliance Intensity | Focus |
|----------|---------------------|-------|
| Food-contact | HIGH | FSSAI, BIS, food-grade certs |
| Cosmetics | HIGH | IS 15778, BIS, labeling |
| Electronics | HIGH | BIS, EMC, safety marks |
| Toys | HIGH | BIS, age-appropriate, safety |
| Decorative | LOW | HSN only |
| Hardware | LOW | HSN, maybe load ratings |
| Apparel | MEDIUM | Fiber content, care labels |

---

## HSN CODE RESEARCH

### What is HSN?

Harmonized System of Nomenclature - standardized classification for GST and trade:
- 4-digit: Chapter and heading
- 6-digit: Subheading
- 8-digit: Tariff item (India-specific)

### HSN Research Strategy

### HSN Research Strategy (Parallel)

Instead of stepping 1-2-3, fire a broad volley:

```
[Volley 1: HSN Discovery]
   |--> Query: "[product] [material] HSN code India GST"
   |--> Query: "HSN [likely_chapter] [product] classification"
   |--> Query: "[product] GST rate India"
```

**Synthesis:** Combine results to confirm Code + Rate + Description.

### Common HSN Chapters

| Chapter | Category | Examples |
|---------|----------|----------|
| 39 | Plastics | PET, PP, HDPE containers |
| 70 | Glass | Bottles, jars, glassware |
| 73 | Iron/Steel | Hardware, fixtures |
| 74 | Copper | Brass items (copper alloy) |
| 83 | Base metal miscellaneous | Mountings, fittings |
| 69 | Ceramics | Pottery, tableware |
| 94 | Furniture | Furniture, furnishings |

### HSN Implications

Every HSN code has implications beyond classification:
- GST rate (5%, 12%, 18%, 28%)
- Import duty (if applicable)
- Export incentives (some HSN codes qualify)
- Compliance triggers (food-contact HSN = FSSAI relevant)

---

## CERTIFICATION REQUIREMENTS

### India-Specific Certifications

| Certification | Full Name | Required For |
|---------------|-----------|--------------|
| BIS | Bureau of Indian Standards | Mandatory products list |
| FSSAI | Food Safety and Standards Authority | Food and food-contact |
| ISI | Indian Standards Institution | Quality mark (voluntary) |
| BEE | Bureau of Energy Efficiency | Appliances |
| WPC | Wireless Planning & Coordination | RF devices |
| CDSCO | Central Drugs Standard Control | Medical devices |

### Food-Contact Certification Matrix

| Material | Use Case | Required Certs |
|----------|----------|----------------|
| PET | Food storage | Food-grade, BPA-free claim |
| Glass | Food/beverage | Generally safe, check lead-free |
| Stainless Steel | Cookware | Food-grade steel (304/316) |
| Plastic lids | Food containers | Food-grade PP/HDPE |
| Ceramics | Tableware | Lead/cadmium-free for food use |

### Certification Research Queries

**Query Pattern:** `[product type] [material] compliance India [regulation body]`
**Query Pattern:** `[product type] BIS mandatory registration`
**Query Pattern:** `[material] food-grade certification India`

---

## INDUSTRY STANDARDS

### When Standards Matter

| Situation | Standard Relevance |
|-----------|-------------------|
| B2B sales | Buyers expect standard compliance |
| Export | International standards required |
| Premium positioning | Standards validate quality claims |
| Liability products | Safety standards non-negotiable |

### Common Indian Standards

| Standard | Covers |
|----------|--------|
| IS 10146 | Polyethylene containers |
| IS 10909 | PET containers |
| IS 15778 | Cosmetic containers |
| IS 16739 | Packaged water bottles |
| IS 4693 | Stainless steel cookware |

### Standard Research Queries

**Query Pattern:** `IS standard [product type] [material] India`
**Query Pattern:** `[product type] quality standards India BIS`

---

## SPECIAL CATEGORIES

### Handicraft Exemptions

Some handmade items qualify for reduced GST:
- Requires EPCH certification
- Must be individually crafted
- Machine-made disqualified even if artisanal-looking

**Query Pattern:** `handicraft GST exemption India EPCH certification`

### Import/Export Implications

For products that may be imported or exported:
- Duty drawback eligibility
- Quality Control Order (QCO) requirements
- Pre-shipment inspection requirements

**Query Pattern:** `[product type] export compliance India`

