## OUTPUT STRUCTURE

### Compliance Section Format

```markdown
## Classification & Compliance

### HSN Classification
- Code: [8-digit HSN]
- Description: [What this code covers]
- GST Rate: [X%]
- Implications: [What this means for the product]

### Certification Requirements
| Certification | Required? | Why | How to Obtain |
|---------------|-----------|-----|---------------|
| [Cert name] | [Yes/No/Recommended] | [Reason] | [Brief process] |

### Compliance Notes
- [Any special considerations]
- [B2B vs B2C differences]
- [Warnings or conditions]
```

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

### Wrong: Over-researching Non-compliance Products

```
WRONG:
Product: Brass decorative hook
Research: FSSAI, BIS, EMC, food-safety...
(Decorative items have minimal compliance needs!)

RIGHT:
Product: Brass decorative hook
Research: HSN code only (8302 - base metal mountings)
Note: No compliance requirements for decorative hardware
```

### Wrong: Stopping at HSN

```
WRONG:
"HSN 3923, 18% GST"
(What does this MEAN?)

RIGHT:
"HSN 3923 (plastic articles for packing/conveyance), 18% GST.
This classification indicates that for food-contact use,
food-grade certification becomes relevant for B2B buyers.
FSSAI registration required if marketed as food storage."
```

### Wrong: Assuming Compliance

```
WRONG:
"No compliance needed" (without checking)

RIGHT:
"Checked BIS mandatory registration list - this category
not currently mandated. However, food-contact use would
trigger food-grade expectations from buyers."
```

### Wrong: Missing Use-Case Implications

```
WRONG:
"Glass bottle HSN 7010"

RIGHT:
"HSN depends on use case:
- Utility/storage: 7010 (glass containers)
- Cosmetic/perfumery: 3303 (if marketed as such)
- Food/beverage: 7010 but FSSAI relevant
The cork stopper suggests cosmetic positioning - verify intended use."
```

